# Folders' reading and making of archives (zip, 7z and more): the reasons given when one will not open, unpack or be made (src/files/archive.rs).

folders-archive-trouble-locked = it is locked with a password
folders-archive-trouble-wrong-key = that password does not open it
folders-archive-trouble-wrong-or-bad = that password does not open it, or the archive is damaged
folders-archive-trouble-locked-rar = it is a RAR locked with a password, which Folders cannot unlock; nothing is wrong with the file
folders-archive-trouble-locked-foreign = it is locked with a password and packed a way Folders cannot unlock
folders-archive-trouble-unknown = it is not an archive Folders can open
folders-archive-trouble-too-many = it holds more than a million things, more than Folders will unpack
folders-archive-trouble-no-room = there is not room here for what it holds
folders-archive-trouble-gave-up = it needs more memory or time to read than Folders allows
folders-archive-trouble-no-reader = the part of Trindle that reads this kind is missing, and installing updates puts it back
folders-archive-trouble-foreign = it is packed a way Folders cannot read
folders-archive-trouble-parts = a part of it is missing, and every part has to be in the same folder
folders-archive-why-damaged = it is damaged or cut short
folders-archive-why-no-room = there is no room left
folders-archive-why-read-only = nothing can be written in that folder
folders-archive-why-gone = it is not there any more
folders-archive-why-memory = it needs more memory to read than Folders allows
folders-archive-why-other = it could not be read
folders-archive-inside-too-big = too big to open from inside the archive
folders-archive-inside-missing = not in the archive
folders-archive-7z-memory = this 7z needs more memory to unpack than Folders will give it
folders-archive-pack-grew = a file grew too big while it was being packed
folders-archive-pack-exists = there is already something with that name
folders-archive-pack-no-name = nothing to name it by
folders-archive-pack-cannot-make = Folders opens archives of this kind but does not make them

